# Trivy Vulnerability Ignore File
# This file contains vulnerabilities that are being intentionally ignored
# Each entry should include a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore

# ##################### Example ################################
# This example shows the documentation format for npm package vulnerabilities

# CVE-YYYY-NNNNN - Brief vulnerability description [STATUS]
# Affects: package@version (dependency of tool)
# Issue: Technical description of the vulnerability
# Risk: LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH - Risk assessment with justification
# Status: ACTIVE/RESOLVED - Current status with explanation
# Fixed Versions: version range that fixes the issue
# Timeline:
#   - YYYY-MM-DD: Initial discovery or CVE added
#   - YYYY-MM-DD: Status update or resolution
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: URL to package or tracking issue
#   - Verify: Command to check version
# Review: When/how to re-evaluate
# DO NOT UNCOMMENT - This is an example for documentation purposes
# CVE-YYYY-NNNNN

# ############################## End of example ##################################

# Last reviewed: 2026-05-06 (Versions: Claude Code 2.1.129 binary, OpenCode 1.14.39 binary, ripgrep 15.1.0, UBI9 9.7 base)

# CVE-2026-4878 - libcap TOCTOU race condition in cap_set_file() [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: libcap-2.48-10.el9 (UBI9 base)
# Issue: TOCTOU race between lstat() and setxattr() in cap_set_file() allows
#   local attacker with directory write access to redirect capability updates
#   to attacker-controlled file via symlink swap (CWE-367)
# CVSS: 6.7 MEDIUM (AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) — scored by Red Hat as CNA
# Risk: LOW in this container —
#   - setcap is called once at BUILD TIME only (Dockerfile: setcap cap_sys_time+eip /usr/bin/date)
#   - No process calls cap_set_file() at runtime
#   - Container runs as non-root user aiAssistant with no capability to invoke setcap
#   - Exploit requires local access + directory write + privileged process running setcap — none exist at runtime
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata published. Upstream fixed in libcap 2.78.
#   Red Hat Bugzilla: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2447554
# CISA KEV: Not listed. Active exploitation: None.
# Fixed Versions: upstream 2.78, RHEL 9 pending
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-04-06: Public disclosure on oss-security
#   - 2026-04-09: NVD published
#   - 2026-04-23: Triaged for UBI9 rebase — suppressed (not exploitable at runtime)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-4878
#   - Advisory: GHSA-f78v-p5hx-m7hh
#   - Upstream fix: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libcap/libcap.git/commit/?id=286ace1259992bd0c5d9016715833f2e148ac596
# Review: Patch within 30 days of Red Hat errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-07-22
CVE-2026-4878

# CVE-2026-35385 - OpenSSH scp setuid/setgid bit preservation [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: openssh-8.7p1-48.el9_7, openssh-clients-8.7p1-48.el9_7 (UBI9 base)
# Issue: scp running as root with -O (legacy protocol) without -p (preserve mode)
#   fails to strip setuid/setgid bits from downloaded files, allowing privilege
#   escalation if attacker controls the remote source (CWE-281)
# CVSS: 7.5 HIGH (AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) — scored by MITRE as CNA
# EPSS: 0.00039 (percentile 0.118) — extremely low exploitation probability
# Risk: LOW in this container —
#   - scp is not used anywhere in the container (grep-verified across image/ directory)
#   - Container runs as non-root user aiAssistant — exploit requires root + scp -O
#   - All file transfers use git (SSH/HTTPS) or curl, not scp
#   - Firewall-manager restricts outbound connections to whitelisted domains only
#   - Debian security team classifies this as "Minor issue" (no DSA issued)
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata published. Upstream fixed in OpenSSH 10.3p1.
#   Red Hat Bugzilla: status NEW, priority High, no target milestone assigned
# CISA KEV: Not listed. Active exploitation: None. CISA ADP: not automatable.
# Fixed Versions: upstream 10.3p1, RHEL 9 pending
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-04-02: Disclosed and fixed upstream in OpenSSH 10.3p1
#   - 2026-04-23: Triaged for UBI9 rebase — suppressed (not exploitable in context)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-35385
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35385
#   - Upstream: https://www.openssh.org/releasenotes.html#10.3p1
# Review: Patch within 30 days of Red Hat errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-07-22
CVE-2026-35385

# CVE-2026-33845 - GnuTLS DTLS handshake integer underflow (DoS / OOB read) [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: gnutls-3.8.3-10.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive)
# Issue: Malformed DTLS fragments with zero length and non-zero offset trigger integer
#   underflow during handshake reassembly, causing out-of-bounds read (CWE-191).
#   Enables remote DoS or limited information disclosure via crafted DTLS traffic.
# CVSS: 7.5 HIGH (Red Hat) / 9.1 CRITICAL (NIST) — AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H
# Risk: LOW in this container —
#   - No DTLS server runs in the container; no listener on any UDP port
#   - No client code initiates DTLS connections (claude, opencode, pi, git, curl, ssh
#     all use TCP-based TLS only — DTLS is UDP-only and not used by any tool here)
#   - gnutls is a transitive base-image library, not directly invoked by any workload
#   - Container runs as non-root user aiAssistant
#   - firewall-manager restricts egress to whitelisted HTTPS endpoints
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata published. Standard UBI9 marked "none_available".
#   RHSA-2026:13274 only applies to Red Hat Hardened Images (separate product).
#   Red Hat Bugzilla: 2450624
# CISA KEV: Not listed. Active exploitation: None reported.
# Fixed Versions: Red Hat Hardened Images 3.8.13-1.hum1; standard RHEL 9 pending
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-05-02: RHSA-2026:13274 published (Hardened Images only)
#   - 2026-05-06: Triaged for UBI9 — suppressed (no DTLS surface in container)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-33845
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33845
#   - VEX: https://security.access.redhat.com/data/csaf/v2/vex/2026/cve-2026-33845.json
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-33845

# CVE-2026-33846 - GnuTLS DTLS handshake heap buffer overflow (DoS) [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: gnutls-3.8.3-10.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive)
# Issue: merge_handshake_packet() fails to validate length consistency across DTLS
#   fragments. Crafted fragments with conflicting message_length cause allocation
#   sized to the smaller fragment with writes from the larger one, yielding an
#   out-of-bounds heap write (CWE-130).
# CVSS: 7.5 HIGH — AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H
# Risk: LOW in this container — same reasoning as CVE-2026-33845:
#   - No DTLS surface (server or client) anywhere in the image
#   - gnutls is transitive base-image dependency, not invoked at runtime
#   - Container runs as non-root user aiAssistant; firewall-manager restricts egress
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata published. Standard UBI9 marked "none_available".
#   RHSA-2026:13274 only applies to Red Hat Hardened Images (separate product).
#   Red Hat Bugzilla: 2450625
# CISA KEV: Not listed. Active exploitation: None reported.
# Fixed Versions: Red Hat Hardened Images 3.8.13-1.hum1; standard RHEL 9 pending
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-05-02: RHSA-2026:13274 published (Hardened Images only)
#   - 2026-05-06: Triaged for UBI9 — suppressed (no DTLS surface in container)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-33846
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33846
#   - VEX: https://security.access.redhat.com/data/csaf/v2/vex/2026/cve-2026-33846.json
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-33846

# CVE-2026-40356 - MIT krb5 NegoEx integer underflow (DoS) [NO FIX AVAILABLE]
# Affects: krb5-libs-1.21.1-9.el9_7 (UBI9 base, transitive via openssh-clients)
# Issue: Integer underflow in gss_accept_sec_context() when NegoEx mechanism is
#   registered allows unauthenticated remote attacker to trigger out-of-bounds
#   read and crash the process (CWE-191).
# CVSS: 5.9 MEDIUM (NIST) / HIGH (Red Hat) — AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H
# Risk: LOW in this container —
#   - No GSSAPI/Kerberos server; nothing in the image calls gss_accept_sec_context()
#   - NegoEx mechanism not registered (stock UBI9 minimal /etc/gss/mech config) —
#     Red Hat's own recommended workaround is satisfied by default
#   - Container performs no Kerberos auth: git uses HTTPS or SSH keys, ssh uses keys,
#     no kinit, no AD integration, no SPNEGO consumers
#   - krb5-libs is transitive (openssh-clients dep), not invoked at runtime
#   - Container runs as non-root user aiAssistant with no listener on Kerberos ports
# Status: ACTIVE - No RHEL 9 errata published. Standard UBI9 marked "none_available".
#   RHSA-2026:12220 only applies to Red Hat Hardened Images (separate product).
# CISA KEV: Not listed. Active exploitation: None reported.
# Fixed Versions: upstream krb5 1.22.3; RHEL 9 pending
# Timeline:
#   - 2026-04-27: Public analysis published (cems.fun)
#   - 2026-04-30: RHSA-2026:12220 issued for Hardened Images only
#   - 2026-05-06: Triaged for UBI9 — suppressed (NegoEx not registered, no GSSAPI
#     accept-side calls in container)
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-40356
#   - NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40356
#   - Upstream fix: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/2e75f0d9362fb979f5fc92829431a590a130929f
# Review: Patch within 30 days of RHEL 9 errata, or re-evaluate by 2026-08-04
CVE-2026-40356
